       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg per dose four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day, which is five times the usual maximum for ibuprofen. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for outpatients and 2,400 mg/day in most inpatient protocols. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common analgesic or anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common upper-range dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf 4000 mg per dose is what you intend, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. Then I'll go over the order with you again before I submit it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
