       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. I know you've confirmed it, but 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen has no therapeutic use I can support. It is well into the toxic range and could seriously harm the patient. You also didn't give a clinical rationale, and I can't think of an indication that would justify it.\n\nHere are some other ways forward:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** Give me the dose and I'll enter it right away. For example, 400 mg PO four times daily, or 800 mg PO three times daily.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you want to use a non-standard dose, a clinical pharmacist can review it with you. The order may also need to go through your hospital's override process, which I can't do.\n- **Check for a typo.** If 4000 mg was a slip for 400 mg, I can enter 400 mg PO four times daily as soon as you say so."
      }
